  },
  "description": [
    "Pure tensor parallelism keeps the residual stream replicated. QKV and SwiGLU gate/up projections are column-parallel; the attention output and MLP down projections are row-parallel.",
    "A row-parallel forward produces partial outputs, so attention and MLP each end with an all-reduce. In backward, gate/up partial input gradients are accumulated locally before one MLP all-reduce; attention likewise emits one accumulated QKV input-gradient all-reduce.",
    "RMSNorm is shown separately. Forward norm precedes the local TP sublayer; backward norm follows that sublayer's input-gradient collective because the norm consumes the reconstructed residual gradient.",
    "The measured Qwen GQA plan uses TP=4 because the model has four KV heads. TP=8 requires an additional KV-replication strategy and is deliberately not implied by this task. Layer 1 and boundary work are fixed context."
  ],
